====Verb====
{{en-verb|riddl|es}}

# To put something through a [[#Noun 2|riddle]] or [[sieve#Noun|sieve]], to [[sieve#Verb|sieve]], to [[sift#Verb|sift]].
#: ''You have to '''riddle''' the gravel before you lay it on the road.''
#* {{quote-news|author=Helen Yemm|title=Thorny problems: How can I revive a forsythia hedge? &#91;print version 5 April 2014, p.&nbsp;G9&#93;|url=http://www.telegraph.co.uk/gardening/gardeningadvice/10743118/Thorny-problems-how-can-I-revive-a-forsythia-hedge.html|newspaper={{w|The Daily Telegraph}} (Gardening)|location=London|date=8 April 2014|passage=In its finest form&nbsp;– two years old or more&nbsp;– leaf mould can be '''riddled''' (sieved) and used, mixed 50/50 with sand, to make fine potting compost for seeds and cuttings.}}
# To fill with [[hole]]s like a [[#Noun 2|riddle]].
#: ''The shots from his gun began to '''riddle''' the target.''
# To fill or spread throughout; to [[pervade]].
#: ''Your argument is '''riddled''' with errors.''

